# Line endings.
#
# Without this file, git stores whatever bytes the working tree happens to
# contain. A file rewritten by a different editor then shows as every line
# changed. On 16 Aug 2026 `git status` listed 38 modified files here, of which
# 11 had actually changed — the other 27, including every Platforms/ file and
# the .sln, differed only by carriage returns.
#
# text=auto stores every text file with LF in the repository and checks it out
# with the platform's own endings, so Visual Studio keeps working and the
# history stays readable.
* text=auto

# Visual Studio rewrites these with CRLF whenever it touches them. Pinning the
# checkout stops them reappearing as modified after every solution load.
*.sln text eol=crlf
*.csproj text eol=crlf

*.cs text diff=csharp
*.xaml text
*.svg text

# Never transformed.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
